flex_attention_bwd: always append safe fallback configs.

The shared-memory estimator underestimates real usage for some configs:
measured on sm_120 (RTX 5070 Ti, 101376 B shared memory per SM) with
block=64, num_stages=1, head_dim=256, bf16 the kernel actually requires
114688 B while the formula estimates 75776 B. The needs_patch gate then
accepted torch's sm12x default FlexBwDConfig(64,64,64,64,1,4) as the
ONLY candidate, so inductor never benchmarked alternatives and training
died at kernel launch:

    InductorError: RuntimeError: No valid triton configs.
    OutOfMemoryError: out of resource: ...flex_attention_backward...
    Required: 114688 Hardware limit: 101376

The estimator cannot prove a config safe, so drop the gate and always
append the fallback configs: with more than one candidate inductor
benchmarks them at compile time and prunes the OOM ones.
--- a/unsloth_zoo/temporary_patches/flex_attention_bwd.py	2026-07-06 19:43:50.640525481 +0200
+++ b/unsloth_zoo/temporary_patches/flex_attention_bwd.py	2026-07-06 19:43:50.659330187 +0200
@@ -104,17 +104,12 @@
                 except Exception:
                     configs = []
 
-                # Patch only if some original config exceeds shared memory.
-                needs_patch = False
-                for c in configs:
-                    max_block = max(c.block_m1, c.block_n1, c.block_m2, c.block_n2)
-                    est = _estimate_shmem(max_block, c.num_stages, head_dim, dtype)
-                    if est > shmem_limit:
-                        needs_patch = True
-                        break
-
-                if not needs_patch and configs:
-                    return configs
+                # The estimator UNDERESTIMATES real usage for some configs
+                # (measured on sm_120: block=64, stages=1, head_dim=256, bf16
+                # -> 114688 B actual vs 75776 B estimated), so it cannot prove
+                # a config safe. Always append fallbacks: with >1 candidates
+                # inductor benchmarks at compile time and prunes OOM configs,
+                # instead of baking a single config that fails at launch.
 
                 # Add safe fallback configs for this GPU / head_dim / dtype
                 safe = _generate_safe_configs(FlexBwDConfig, shmem_limit, head_dim, dtype)
